A few weeks ago, we started investigating the possibility of
putting Linux on an XBOX. We played with some ideas in our heads,
  a render farm, a cheap office computer or a distributed crypto
platform, just to start. The idea required a little bit of elbow
grease, a mod chip, Linux and a bunch of free time.

All XBOXes are locked into only booting the Microsoft BIOS. That
is, if you buy a new XBOX, it's basic IO does not let you do all
that much, except read DVDs, and XBOX games that have special
keys encoded into them. A mod chip is a computer chip with another
BIOS that physically overrides the Microsoft BIOS....

